{"full":"hf:build-small-hackathon/open-cortex","spaceId":"build-small-hackathon/open-cortex","name":"OpenCortex","source":"huggingface","description":"Feel a local LLM think,  work, and forget.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","track:backyard-ai","sponsor:openbmb","sponsor:nvidia","sponsor:modal","achievement:offgrid","achievement:offbrand","achievement:llama","backyard-ai","off-brand","tiny-titan","best-demo","codex","llama-cpp","local-ai","ai-infra","observability","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":4,"created":"2026-06-15T13:19:25.000Z","updated":"2026-06-16T14:15:12.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://build-small-hackathon-open-cortex.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/open-cortex","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:49:39.340Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:49:39.340Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:49:39.340Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🧠","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OpenCortex is a real-time observatory for local LLM inference. It pairs a chat interface with a living view of the runtime behind the answer: working memory, context pressure, token flow, and engine health.","It is built for learners, local AI users, and AI infrastructure engineers who want to understand why an LLM slows down, loops, forgets, or runs out of context.","Small local models make AI personal again. But local inference is still a black box for most users. When a response becomes slow or repetitive, the user rarely knows whether the model is thinking, overloaded, stuck in a loop, or simply running out of context."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/open-cortex/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a0306da6eff38595284edc33490dfe4c73633133c68e7714333782873db1c947","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:10.365Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:49:39.372Z","projectInsight